Why these factor forms:
- Budget-normalized attacker strength -> apples-to-apples across attack styles; strength is a controllable, continuous-ish knob with monotone effect expectation → allows clean estimation of the interaction with defense.
- Ordinal defense ladder within a single family → the "strength" dimension is truly ordinal and monotonic; avoids confounding type vs strength.
- Previously tested tricks binary → captures the "combined jailbreak technique" notion: adding known tricks on top of base attack; keep binary for power and interpretability; sub-analysis per individual trick.

Why full factorial 2×2×3×2=24:
- Main goal includes interaction dynamics (A×B especially). Full factorial is required to estimate two-way interactions without aliasing (fractional would alias A×B with other effects).
- Repeated over 2 datasets with the same prompts → blocked/pared design → more power, allows within-prompt estimation, and enables dataset-level interaction checks.
- 24 cells is manageable, and each cell is an analysis unit on N prompts; full factorial beats fractional here because interaction of primary interest is exactly what a fractional design would sacrifice (aliasing).

